hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22836","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Abu az-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Nuaym ibn Hammar al-Ghatafani, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: O son of Adam, do not fail in four rakahs from the beginning of the day; I will suffice you its end."
"22837","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Said, meaning Ibn Abdul-Aziz, narrated to us: Makhul narrated to us, from Nuaym ibn Hammar al-Ghatafani, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: O son of Adam, do not fail in four rakahs from the beginning of the day; I will suffice you its end."
"22838","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Zayd, meaning Thabit ibn Yazid, narrated to us, from Bard, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Ibn Murrah, from Qays al-Judhami, from Nuaym, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: O son of Adam, pray for Me four rakahs at the beginning of the day; I will suffice you its end."
"22839","Abu an-Nadr and Abdus-Samad said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Nuaym ibn Hammar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Your Lord, mighty and majestic, said: Pray for Me, O son of Adam, four in the beginning of the day; I will suffice you its end."
"22840","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Said ibn Abdul-Aziz informed me, from Makhul, from Ibn Murrah, from Nuaym ibn Hammar al-Ghatafani, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: O son of Adam, pray for Me four rakahs from the beginning of the day; I will suffice you its end."
"22841","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us: Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu az-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Nuaym ibn Hammar, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Son of Adam, do not fail in four rakahs at the beginning of the day; I will suffice you its end."
"22842","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rashid ad-Dimashqi narrated to us: Makhul narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Nuaym ibn Hammar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your Lord, blessed and exalted, said: Son of Adam, pray for Me four rakahs at the beginning of the day; I will suffice you its end. There is no man in Sham sounder in hadith than Said ibn Abdul-Aziz."
"22843","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Nuaym ibn Hammar, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which martyrs are best? He said: Those who, if they meet the ranks, turn their faces until they are killed; those will go in the highest chambers of Paradise, and their Lord will laugh to them, and when your Lord laughs to a servant in this world, there is no reckoning upon him."
